---
import Layout from "~/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Link from "~/components/Link.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="nv-page-title">
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl">Advocacy Resources For Outside Pen Pals</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6">
    <p>
      One of PCP’s goals as a prisoner solidarity project is to build our
      collective capacity to fight for prisoners on an individual and structural
      level. We want to empower outside pen pals to advocate for comrades in
      prison.
    </p>

    <p>
      If your pen pal is facing abuse or needs support from the outside, but you
      don’t know where to start, please get in touch with us!
    </p>

    <div class="wp-block-kadence-spacer aligncenter kt-block-spacer-7899_eb1be3-8d">
      <div class="kt-block-spacer kt-block-spacer-halign-center">
        <hr class="kt-divider" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
      How to write a letter of support for parole/clemency/asylum
    </h2>

    <!-- TODO: restore resources -->
    <div class="wp-block-file">
      <a
        id="wp-block-file--media-f3ba3efa-78c3-4ff0-9ad5-f86e47acb3fe"
        href="/docs/advocacy-resources-tips-for-writing-support-letters-for-clemency-or-parole.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        Tips for Writing Support Letters for Clemency or Parole – by Jennifer
        Rose
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="wp-block-file">
      <a
        id="wp-block-file--media-76d07ea9-0b3d-41c8-a6ef-5fd1f3c7be63"
        href="/docs/advocacy-resources-letters-of-support.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        Letters of Support – by Shawn Crabtree
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="wp-block-heading">Organizing a phone zap/campaign</h2>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://incarceratedworkers.org/resources/how-organize-phone-zap"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        How to Organize a Phone Zap – Incarcerated Workers Organizing Committee
      </a>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://prisonhealth.news/2019/03/10/how-loved-ones-outside-can-advocate-for-people-in-prison/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        How Loved Ones Outside Can Advocate for People in&nbsp;Prison – Prison
        Health News
      </a>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://www.prisonpolicy.org/trainings/"
        data-type="URL"
        data-id="https://www.prisonpolicy.org/trainings/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        Advocacy Toolkit – Prison Policy Initiative
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
      Find out about a prison/DOC’s specific policies
    </h2>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://www.prisoncensorship.info/prisonprofiles"
        data-type="URL"
        data-id="https://www.prisoncensorship.info/prisonprofiles"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
      >
        Info on US Prisons by State and Facility – MIM(Prisons)
      </a>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a
        rel="noreferrer noopener"
        href="https://tlcenter.app.box.com/s/szt8awqsh9dnjqgu0n0hgfjxac6fzy9m"
        data-type="URL"
        data-id="https://tlcenter.app.box.com/s/szt8awqsh9dnjqgu0n0hgfjxac6fzy9m"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Agency-Specific Policies – Transgender Law Center
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="wp-block-kadence-spacer aligncenter kt-block-spacer-7899_08e740-a6">
      <div class="kt-block-spacer kt-block-spacer-halign-center">
        <hr class="kt-divider" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      See also our
      <Link href="/product/the-word-is-out-20">2018 newsletter</Link>, which
      features writing from PCP inside members on the subject of censorship, and
      our
      <Link href="/product/the-word-is-out-23">2021 newsletter</Link>
      about healthcare.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you have experience with prisoner advocacy from inside or outside, feel
      free to share your own personal testimony or resources that you have found
      helpful.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
